      "text": "\\begin{align\\*}\n             |{-4+ti}| &= \\sqrt{(-4)^2+t^2} \\\\\n             &= \\sqrt{16+t^2} \\\\\n             &=2\\sqrt{13} \\\\\n              \\Rightarrow t^2 &=68 \\\\\n              \\Rightarrow| t | &=\\pm \\sqrt{68}\n              \\end{align\\*}\nSo $t$ has two positive value and $t = \\boxed{8\\sqrt{2}}$\n=====\n\nnote: I have erased some parts in your solution mainly because I don't want to tell you how to obtain them, but you can try to see this technique applied on your own problem (this should be called \"*factorization*\" I think  :P ) , and to use Kroneker Delta (this is something that you may have learned about as the square of a number equals its transpose (which in turn equals the original number) and the same equation will also be true for the scalar product of two numbers (this will, no doubt, give you an idea on the idea of transpose when it comes to matrices).)",
