      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "First, calculate the magnitude of the complex number $-4+ti$.\n\\[|-4+ti|=\\sqrt{(-4)^2+ti^2}= \\sqrt{16+t^2}\\]\n\nAccording to the given problem, the magnitude should be $2\\sqrt{13}$.\n\\[2\\sqrt{13}= \\sqrt{16+t^2}\\]\n\nSquare both sides to remove the square root:\n\\[36+16t^2=504\\]\n\nOnce more to make calculations simpler:\n\\[16t^2=468\\]\n\nSolve for $t$:\n\\[t^2=\\frac{468}{16}\\]\n\nFinally, take the square root of both sides:\n\\[t=\\frac{\\sqrt{468}}{\\sqrt{16}}\\]\n\\[t=\\boxed{3\\sqrt{6}}\\]",
